# The repo is edited on Windows and RUNS on Linux — WSL for the rehearsal,
# `apify/actor-python:3.12` in the cloud. Anything Linux executes must keep LF
# endings, or the kernel reads the shebang as `/usr/bin/env bash\r` and answers:
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# Measured 2026-08-20 on `run_local.sh`, the documented deploy rehearsal — the
# one command DEPLOY.md tells you to run before pushing. It had been committed
# with CRLF and could not start at all under WSL.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.timer         text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf

# Python is safe either way (the interpreter accepts both), but the actor image
# and the Windows checkout should not disagree about file contents.
*.py            text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
